  "review_note": "Read the test and helper line by line. (1) Oracle is independent: Henderson tabular A built by hand from an inbred pedigree (I checked on Totoro that its offspring diag(A)-1 is 0.25/0.375/0.5/0.59375/0.671875, the full-sib inbreeding recursion, and that it is symmetric and positive definite); the 2m x 2m covariance (S_k S_l R_kl A) and the dense joint-Newton Laplace with hand-derived logit/probit/cloglog derivatives are base R, and the link terms are checked against dbinom and central differences. (a) The Julia fit ESTIMATES the shared correlation: the contract and the existing q2 test show rho = tanh(eta_rho) as a free parameter (atanh_rho); the test reads it from fit$corpars$mu 'cor((Intercept),x | id)' and the oracle uses that fitted rho. It is not fixed at 0: flipping its sign moves the oracle by 2.4 to 12.7 log-units, and a rho of 0 would have made that gap 0 and failed the test. Layout is one animal field, one correlated term, q=2, coefficient-specific scales (sd formulas on both (Intercept) and x), so the row mechanism is the one named. Both targets (mu:I, mu:x1) have their own selector and own reversed-SD bug. All three providers were fitted separately (A x3 links, Ainv logit, pedigree x3 links), which matches the 14 row keys exactly (6 + 2 + 6). (2) Bug sensitivity asserted at >20x tolerance; smallest measured gap 0.4486 (449x), and every one of 9 emulated bugs was asserted. (4) All sha256 values (receipt, manifest, test, helper, 6 source files, console log) match current files; HEAD 996eccf79 matches the receipt; console log shows 142 passed, 0 failed, 0 errors, 0 skips and 'Julia bridge: 1 live test ran'. Totoro native rerun of this file gives 0 passed, 1 skipped (no live Julia there), so counts rest on the Mac console log, which I did not rerun. Does NOT establish: that the Julia rho or SD estimates are the maximiser (the oracle is evaluated at the Julia estimates; only beta, a0, a1 are perturbed for one A-logit fit, rho is not); a Julia-versus-exact-marginal claim (Laplace vs Laplace, same approximation); one fixture and one seed per link; no calibration, coverage, SE or interval claim; no other family, q>2, or other pedigree.",
